<article class="env-lemma" id="0DT8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DT8">Lemma <span data-tag="0DT8">39.13.6</span>.</a> Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid over a scheme $S$. Let $S' \to S$ be a morphism. Then the base changes $U' = S' \times _ S U$, $R' = S' \times _ S R$ endowed with the base changes $s'$, $t'$, $c'$ of the morphisms $s, t, c$ form a groupoid scheme $(U', R', s', t', c')$ over $S'$ and the projections determine a morphism $(U', R', s', t', c') \to (U, R, s, t, c)$ of groupoid schemes over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: $R' \times _{s', U', t'} R' = S' \times _ S (R \times _{s, U, t} R)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>